son\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0b50f9ec94964fe8809f82da1ac88aa9c66280a76fd8de3962b88692e0b7fbc1","event_uuid":"5804d333-2144-4a53-9700-7766f15ed681","position":{"commit_sha":"d38b4c3abaec96eb2706aaebb11376b389e7e010","position":"1787094057904920001-5804d333-2144-4a53-9700-7766f15ed681"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6ed0ffa1aff440cff89971b64dc430d54545c11d8664781e727eeabe06347318","event_uuid":"c8d2e8c0-8d63-4c58-9f16-5f003935e745","position":{"commit_sha":"d38b4c3abaec96eb2706aaebb11376b389e7e010","position":"1787094059373660001-c8d2e8c0-8d63-4c58-9f16-5f003935e745"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"dbb34329872664f823fa05e4a04c43286a0c4a68efea0d7f08aad066e6690795","event_uuid":"7e8f171d-02fc-46a5-a688-f95d883de3ad","position":{"commit_sha":"2cbf5f074ae5c7ff5414bc9ffa5e3054f0870a66","position":"1787094405621438001-7e8f171d-02fc-46a5-a688-f95d883de3ad"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"62bb0aaf0ba8614fc9b653ea9827f3aa0b8bd948efcb592f6f8ed4cb4851f356","event_uuid":"de09009e-780f-4c89-8694-ac3a80ca8bdf","position":{"commit_sha":"6f1622ce0bb31ed0d14096b1a6b7bab8ff20bcc4","position":"1787094414812676001-de09009e-780f-4c89-8694-ac3a80ca8bdf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 1 RCA (confirmed before repair): `tests/conftest.py::_remove_readonly_run_snapshots` materializes `tuple(tmp_path.rglob(\".rebar/run_snapshots\"))`, so it recursively enters every unrelated mutable subtree below a test temp root, including `tests/interfaces/conftest.py::rebar_repo`'s live `repo/.tickets-tracker`. The canonical store write lifecycle intentionally creates and removes `.ticket-write.lock.d` (`src/rebar/_store/lock.py` dual-window contract). Python 3.11 `Path.rglob` caches directory entries from a parent scan and catches `PermissionError` but not `FileNotFoundError` when a cached child vanishes before descent; Python 3.12+ delegates to a walk that ignores the same scandir error. A deterministic runtime barrier used the real `rebar._store.lock.acquire`: after the tracker parent scan cached the live mkdir lock, `LockHandle.release()` removed it; the actual fixture teardown then raised the exact `FileNotFoundError` at `.ticket-write.lock.d` on Python 3.11. The identical barrier returned normally on Python 3.12. This proves canonical lock churn plus the broad mutation-intolerant scan and supported 3.11 traversal semantics are sufficient, while a stable tree or 3.11 alone is not.\n\nThe competing hypothesis that MCP async completion or the lock lifecycle is defective was rejected. Under a real held lock, direct cleanup of an exact `.rebar/run_snapshots` root succeeded and left the lock intact; only the fixture's broad traversal failed when release occurred mid-walk. Async daemon execution and dual-window lock removal are explicit contracts (`src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py`, `src/rebar/_store/lock.py`). Fixture ordering is not causal: direct invocation of the actual fixture reproduced outside pytest fixture scheduling.\n\nDefect legitimacy: Python 3.11 is an explicit supported CI/runtime target (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`, `pyproject.toml`), and closed bug `actinium-civic-needletail` requires shared cleanup of every exact `.rebar/run_snapshots` below test-owned `tmp_path` while preserving unrelated content and read-only publication. Commit `bedfb276...` introduced this regression. Expected repair behavior: retain recursive exact-root coverage and tolerate only unrelated entries that disappear concurrently; do not change workflow async semantics, store locking, snapshot permissions, or mask non-disappearance filesystem errors.","timestamp":1787094405621438001}],"created_at":1787093779924236001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5c9b2d68-f07d-463a-9481-5349b6ddea78","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"9bb7-4430-1202-4d93"}],"description":"## Context\nGerrit 1876 patch set 2, GitHub Actions run 32193981982, Ubuntu Python 3.11 job 95894688032 failed after 13,892 tests passed. The session teardown fixture `tests/conftest.py::_remove_readonly_run_snapshots` evaluated `tuple(tmp_path.rglob(\".rebar/run_snapshots\"))`; traversal entered `repo/.tickets-tracker/.ticket-write.lock.d`, which disappeared during recursion, and `pathlib` raised `FileNotFoundError`. The failing node was `tests/interfaces/store/test_workflow_entrypoints.py::test_mcp_run_workflow_is_async_and_pollable`.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce the traversal failure with a deterministic barrier while separating three rivals: Python/pathlib version semantics, concurrent mkdir-lock churn, and fixture scope over the whole pytest temp tree.\n- Establish defect legitimacy and caller impact from the teardown contract and prior read-only snapshot cleanup bug.\n- Design a held-out race oracle at the smallest tier that executes the production teardown helper with real concurrent filesystem mutation; prove final-form RED.\n- Repair only the confirmed mechanism, then prove held-out GREEN, exact-defect mutation RED, and original-scenario replication.\n- Sweep all live recursive teardown scans for the same disappearing-entry hazard and disposition any siblings.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A runtime experiment deterministically proves the root cause and rejects pathlib-version-only and unrelated-fixture explanations.\n- [ ] A gating regression test uses a deterministic synchronization barrier, reaches the disappearing-directory state, and asserts cleanup completes without masking unrelated filesystem errors.\n- [ ] The final-form oracle is observed RED before repair, GREEN after a held-out repair, and RED again under an exact-defect mutation.\n- [ ] Focused fixture/workflow tests, the broad relevant test gate, lint, and typecheck pass.\n- [ ] All live recursive teardown scans are audited and every confirmed sibling is fixed or ticketed.\n- [ ] The CI scenario no longer reproduces under repeated synchronized churn.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/conftest.py","reason":"repair shared teardown discovery to tolerate concurrent disappearing directories on supported Python 3.11"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_snapshot_fixture_cleanup.py","reason":"strengthen existing cleanup regression with deterministic real-lock race oracle and error-boundary control"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"5804d333-2144-4a53-9700-7766f15ed681","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","flaky","tests","concurrency"],"ticket_id":"26b5-5806-f5ea-4ee8","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Snapshot teardown rglob races disappearing tracker lock directory","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ae46efe5-4649-4f25-a383-f4e0d6508a82","5c9b2d68-f07d-463a-9481-5349b6ddea78","b50a40ee-0108-4a8a-bd8b-62491901449a","222b0ec0-d492-4ccb-889c-f5de29495690","5804d333-2144-4a53-9700-7766f15ed681","c8d2e8c0-8d63-4c58-9f16-5f003935e745","7e8f171d-02fc-46a5-a688-f95d883de3ad","de09009e-780f-4c89-8694-ac3a80ca8bdf"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787094414812676002,"uuid":"1530c699-ec68-49dd-a935-3a6e7e221f4d"}